  "question": "Do the already-located NDL physical targets for 2011 《赵万里文集》第1卷 p.197 and the 1951 《文物参考资料》第9期 pp.221–233 have a lawful remote-copy route that can be closed at the official policy layer without logging in, paying, or pretending the pages were directly reviewed?",
  "answer": "Yes at the NDL service-policy layer, but no page acquisition has occurred. NDL official rules make NDL holdings generally eligible for paid remote copying subject to listed exclusions, require a registered user and a precise page/article locator, and allow whole-article copying from a sufficiently old periodical while book copying remains partial-work scoped. Both project targets already have exact NDL paper-holding routes and exact locators, so access advances from unadjudicated service eligibility to policy-layer eligible / login-and-fee gated. Exact item acceptance, delivery mode, staff processing and page contents remain unreviewed because no account action, request or payment was made.",
